['10','Return unused inward foreign exchange','Conditional return route','PBOC Article 14 permits non-domestic individuals to return unused foreign exchange received from abroad through the original route, with valid ID.','May fit funds that remain in foreign currency.','Not proof that arbitrary CNY savings can be returned; original trail matters.','pbc'],
['11','Reconvert unused RMB from prior exchange','Limited reconversion route','HSBC requires authentic physical original exchange slip issued within 24 months; cannot exceed original amount. ID-only small cash exceptions: USD 500 equivalent, or USD 1,000 at designated departure locations outside customs control.','Useful for identifiable unused travel/exchange funds.','Not a general large-savings route; cash and original-conversion restrictions.','hsbc pbc'],
['12','Remit existing foreign-currency savings','After-conversion step','HSBC outbound section requires valid ID for remittance from foreign-currency savings; representatives need authorization and both IDs.','May avoid an unnecessary second FX conversion if already USD.','Does not solve CNY purchase eligibility; authenticity checks and bank processing still relevant.','hsbc'],
