taxes=[['Worldwide income','US citizens must report taxable worldwide income; leaving money in China does not itself remove this duty.','world'],['Foreign tax credit','Form 1116 generally used by individuals; only qualifying taxes and applicable limitations. Cannot credit taxes attributable to excluded income.','credit'],['Currency disposition','Section 988 includes dispositions of nonfunctional currency and foreign-currency demand/time deposits. Personal vs investment classification and basis need review; do not assume all principal is taxable or all conversion is tax-free.','988'],['USD translation','IRS generally requires USD determinations and translation when income/expense is received, paid or accrued at the relevant exchange rate. A current bank quote is not necessarily historical tax basis.','fx'],['FBAR','Aggregate foreign financial accounts exceeding USD 10,000 at any time in the calendar year; separate FinCEN filing. Closing/transferring an account later does not erase an earlier threshold crossing (analysis of annual test).','forms'],['Form 8938 · US residence','Single/married separately: more than USD 50,000 year-end or USD 75,000 anytime. Joint: more than USD 100,000 year-end or USD 150,000 anytime; filing conditions apply.','forms'],['Form 8938 · qualifying abroad','Single/married separately: more than USD 200,000 year-end or USD 300,000 anytime. Joint: more than USD 400,000 year-end or USD 600,000 anytime. User’s residence not assumed.','forms'],['Foreign gifts / bequests','IRS describes Form 3520 reporting for more than USD 100,000 from nonresident alien individuals/foreign estates, aggregating related foreign persons. Foreign trusts have separate rules. Do not reclassify owned savings as a gift.','world'],['Outbound tax record filing','Official Shenzhen search excerpt describes certain single outbound payments exceeding USD 50,000; full page retrieval failed. Exact exceptions/application remain unverified here. Filing is not itself evidence of a flat conversion tax.','filing']]
